ls stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast tissue excision  The specimen is oriented  short stitch designates superior  long stitch designates lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  On cross sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white gray firm gritty mass  This mass focally abuts the posterior margin  is 0 1cm from the closest inferior margin 1 0cm from anterior margin  1 5cm from medial margin  2 5cm from lateral margin and 3 5cm from superior margin  Located 0 5cm away from the mass  superior aspect from mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cystic cavity with smooth inner tan pink inner lining which could correspond to previous biopsy site  The remaining breast parenchyma is approximately 50  fibrous tissue and 50  adipose tissue  The fibrous tissue is ill defined and has several small cystic structures  The specimen is submitted as follows  A D  representative sections of the mass with closest margins  E   cystic cavity and its relation to the mass  F H  representative sections of the fibrous tissue away from the mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  inferior half of cavity  shave margins  are two irregular portions of fibrofatty tissue which range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Specimen is not oriented  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes I N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  superior half of cavity  shaved margin  are two irregular pieces of fibrofatty tissue which range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimens are not oriented  They are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes O R  Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST LEFT INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY SHAVED MARGINS  PART C  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY SHAVED MARGIN   , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 30 CLINICAL DATA  Patient has known locally advanced breast carcinoma  with a previous positive sentinel node biopsy  neoadjuvant chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  6  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST   LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL TISSUE    EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 18                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion breast tissue  with 2 undesignated sutures arbitrarily designated as follows  short sutures designating superior  long suture designating lateral  The anterior aspect is black inked  the posterior is blue inked  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 30  dense white fibrous tissue and 70  yellow lobulated fatty tissue  The fibrous tissue extends to the posterior  inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral  A F  fibrous tissue to inferior margin  H I  fibrous tissue to superior margin  J  fibrous tissue to inferior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left node axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue  which is partially surface by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan brown unremarkable irregular skin  There are several tan red rubbery lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in greatest dimension  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan white indurated area  Representative sections are submitted as follows  K  four fragments of tissue    nodes   L  three fragments of tissue    nodes   M  two whole lymph nodes  N  indurated area  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue fragments  which are serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as O S  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SGR                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 03 CLINICAL DATA  Right modified radical mastectomy for stage III ductal carcinoma  Biopsy was positive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  Patient given preoperative chemotherapy  cytoxan  methotrexate  and 5 FU                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA OF BREAST  95    AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    WITH FOCAL COMEDO FEATURES  EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  INTRAMAMMARY AND INTRADERMALLY  20 OF 23 LYMPH NODES ARE POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Areas of tumor are poorly differentiated  Two nodules of metastatic tumor in the axillary fat have no lymphoid architecture and are in addition to the nodes above  Several small veins surrounding some of the lymph nodes also contain intraluminal carcinoma cells  There are several small foci of malignant cells identified at the inked deep resection margin  No pagetoid cells are found in the epidermis on H and E and on PAS stain  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring 15 x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an attached axillary tail measuring 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  There is an overlying ellipse of skin  measuring 16 x 7 cm with a linear depression of skin at the lateral superior areolar margin    scar   Located 5cm from the medial tip of the skin ellipse and 2cm from the superior aspect of the skin ellipse is a 3 0cm areola with a 0 8cm nipple  Underlying the linear depression at the margin of the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrous area  Just deep to this fibrous area is a cream colored  hard mass  2 5cm from the deep resection margin   The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm firm  white yellow mass is apparent in the superomedial deep aspect of the specimen  1 0cm from the proximal deep resection margin   There is a 9 x 9 x 5cm round  fibrous area present beneath the center of the skin ellipse  admixed with fat  SECTION CODE  A G  multiple rubbery to firm  white tan nodules  0 2 to 2 5cm    H K  representative sections of mass underlying fibrous scar  L N  representative sections of mass from the superomedial aspect of the breast  deep   O  grossly normal breast tissue  P  rubbery mass  beneath center of the ellipse   Q  nipple  R  biopsy scar  S X  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  David L Gibbs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Checked.
