Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 02 CLINICAL DATA   REMOVED_CASE_ID  prior left breast  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  breast cancer  Now lump at lumpectomy site with suspicious FNA  Short stitch superior  long stitch lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  WIDE EXCISION  1  RECURRENT INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT AT THE DEEP MARGIN  AND LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE FROM THE SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  3  FAT NEROSIS WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS PROCEDURE SITE  4  FOCAL RADIATION CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The intra operative gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS SKIN  LEFT BREAST   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 4 x 3 x 0 5cm circumscribed breast fragment with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse  Sectioning into the tissue shows a 0 5cm in diameter  ill defined  firm  tan gray nodule abutting the superficial and deep surfaces  away from the medial and lateral surfaces  The nodule and surrounding tissue is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue entirely in D through I  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  SMALL NODULE  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT WIDE EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
