Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 02 CLINICAL DATA  Status post left breast lumpectomy for cancer  now presenting with new right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM INVASIVE CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO MARGIN  THE INTRAOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  A small focus of cauterized carcinoma which may represent a second focus of invasive carcinoma is present away from the main tumor at an inked margin  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast  containing an ill defined tan firm mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  grossly abutting the inked resection margin  A touch prep is obtained from the mass  Sections of the mass are submitted in A D  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable and two random sections are submitted in E and F  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
