say  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 2 0cm specimen of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple soft tan lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes A and G  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Highest axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm soft tan lymph node submitted entirely in cassette H  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right breast reexcision stitch on deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 3 2cm specimen of soft white  tan  yellow tissue with a suture on one side and a REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm attached skin ellipse  The specimen is doubled inked  yellow on the deep aspect  and in cross section reveals a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 2cm ill defined biopsy space that is composed of areas of soft white tan tissue and hemorrhage  Biopsy cavity is submitted entirely in cassette I through T  Resident  Jay Austen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Lyn