value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm red  yellow  firm tissue mass  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm lobulated  tan nodule on cut surface extending to margin  Representative sections frozen as FX 1  saved for estrogen receptors and sent to Cox 5  Received fresh  is a 590 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left modified radical mastectomy consisting of a 10 0cm axillary tail  an REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm skin ellipse with a 5 0cm incision superior to the nipple  The nipple and areolar complex are unremarkable  On cross section underneath the described incision  is a 4 5cm biopsy cavity that comes to within 0 5cm of the closest deep inked margin  The cavity is hemorrhagic  The tissue surrounding the biopsy is firm and white  Toward the lateral aspect of the breast  there is an area of hemorrhage not continuous with the biopsy cavity  SECTION CODE  A  remainder of the nonfrozen tissue from the frozen section  B  superior margin of the biopsy cavity  C  inferior margin of the biopsy cavity  D  anterior half of C  E  lateral margin of the biopsy cavity  F  medial margin of the biopsy cavity  G  more anterior half of F  H  skin half of I  I  representative inferior section adjacent