Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON  06 AUG 01 at 14 03 CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications on left mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE 1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE 1 AND COMMENT  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  ASSOCIATED WITH BENIGN AND NEOPLASTIC COMPONENTS  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED ON C F  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  measured from section E  Grade  1 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior  orange inked  margin of the specimen along a broad front  section E   Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Focally positive at the posterior  orange inked  margin of the specimen  Stains for receptors  Requested  COMMENT  The in situ carcinoma is present in 4 of 7 sections  C F  and has moderate to marked nuclear atypia  It has a secretory and  clinging  pattern in some areas and in other areas is associated with cystically dilated glands with flattened epithelium and thyroid colloid like secretions  This latter component is reminiscent of the appearance of the cystic hypersecretory hyperplasia carcinoma spectrum of lesions  The microcalifications associated with the in situ and invasive carcinomatous components are larger and denser than those within the fibrocystic areas  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR HALF  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF IN SITU OR INVASIVE TUMOR  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR HALF  FINAL SHAVE MARGIN   BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF IN SITU OR INVASIVE TUMOR  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED ON J  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 01 at 20 19 Consulting Pathologist s   Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                      BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block E   Few tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  16 AUG 01 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast with needle localization wire  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch denoting the superior margin and the long stitch denoting the lateral margin  The specimen was inked so that the black ink denoted the lateral margin and the blue ink denoted the medial margin and the red ink denoted the anterior and the orange ink denoted the posterior margin  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a tan white nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm located 0 1cm from the medial margin  Calcifications are grossly not identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A G  from superior to inferior  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins superior cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fragment of breast tissue which is submitted entirely in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins inferior half of cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of red breast tissue which is sectioned and submitted in cassettes I and J  Resident  CHRISTINE GARCIA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Joseph Dineen  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR HALF  FINAL MARGIN  PART C  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR HALF  FINAL MARGIN  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 46 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision  right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  RARE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan to yellow soft tissue mass  with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse with 3 5cm centrally well healed scar  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity surrounded by multiple areas of fibrofatty tissue and fat necrosis  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm white to grey  hard nodule 2 5cm from the biopsy cavity  There are surrounding firm white areas radiating from the nodule away from the skin and approaching and abutting the inked resection margin  The nodule is 1 0cm from the nearest resection margin  The biopsy cavity is 1 5cm from the nearest resection margin  SECTION CODE  A  skin ellipse  representative section B  suspicious nodule  representative section C D  suspicious tissue surrounding the nodule and abutting the resection margin  representative section E  biopsy cavity  representative section F J  remainder of suspicious nodule  ess  K  suspicious tissue under skin ellipse An X ray with needle localization accompanies the specimen  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
