f frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue with short stitch on superior and long stitch on lateral margin  Lateral margin is inked red  the remainder inked black  The tissue is serially sectioned from superior to inferior  Sectioning reveals a 1 0cm stellate  tan  firm area with a central depression  Representative sections frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The rest of the breast parenchyma is submitted in A through K  with the firm stellate area in C through F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the new inferior margin  The new inferior margin is inked red and the remaining tissue is inked black  submitted entirely in L through O  medially to laterally  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                 