g consistent with fat necrosis and hemorrhage  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the candidate biopsy cavity to the closest black inked margin  0 9cm   as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  anterior margin left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast tissue  with a suture designating the new margin  The side opposite the suture is tan red and hemorrhagic  The side with the suture consists of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  and is now inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable adipose tissue with areas of hemorrhage and lightening consistent with fat necrosis  The black inked margin is 0 3cm from the closest candidate biopsy cavity  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains performed on the anterior margin specimen show positive staining for E cadherin  and negative staining for keratin REMOVED_DATE and keratin 903 in the proliferative foci  further supporting the diagnosis of DCIS  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MARGIN SUPERIOR POSTERIOR   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  MARGIN ANTERIOR   EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
