ast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 40     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are three separate specimens  Labeled   1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of breast with a palpable lump  Short suture superior  long at lateral  Inked as follows  lateral black  medial blue  posterior green  superior red  inferior yellow  anterior black  Sectioned from deep to superficial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm firm white stellate firm gritty mass that comes to between 0 2cm of the medial  lateral and superior margins and 0 3cm of the posterior  bone  and inferior margin  The superficial  anterior  margin is more than 1 0cm away from the mass  A hemorrhagic area with FNA site anterior to the mass  Mass in relation to the superomedial margin frozen as FX 1  Mass and superolateral margin frozen as FX 3  Labeled   2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy specimen containing a bilobed  well circumscribed  rubbery  tan mass with focal dense calcification  A representative section is frozen as FX 2  Section code  Specimen  1  A  FX 1 C  FX 3 D  Posterior en face E F  Representative slide of mass  bisected G H  Representative slide of mass  bisected I  Representative     including FNA site Specimen  2  B   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  J   section adjacent to that of FX  2  K L  Reminder of specimen labeled  2  Entirely submitted  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new superior margin suture on true margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of focally cauterized  firm  friable adipose tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the new true superior margin  The sutured side is inked black  the opposite blue  Sectioning reveals a firm  white  cut surface with no grossly identifiable lesions  Specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes M O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new inferior margin suture on true margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of breast parenchyma with a suture on one side designating the new inferior margin  The sutured side is inked black  the opposite blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma with no discrete lesions  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes P Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  deep posterior margin suture on true margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of breast parenchyma with a suture on one aspect designating the deep posterior margin  The sutured side is inked black  the opposite blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm  white parenchyma with no discrete lesions  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes R T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new medial margin suture on true margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the new medial margin  The sutured aspect is inked black  the opposite blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma  The specimen has no discrete lesions and is submitted entirely in cassettes U V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new lateral margin suture on true margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the new lateral margin  The sutured side is inked black  the opposite blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm  white  dense parenchyma  No discrete nodules are noted  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes W Z  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary tissue right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes  11  are identified  ranging from 0 2cm in greatest dimension to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  A representative section from each lymph node is submitted entirely in cassettes AA EE  Note that several of the lymph nodes have a firm  white  cut surface suggestive of metastatic carcinoma  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSES  1 AND  3  BREAST  BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  COMING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SECOND SPECIMEN  BENIGN HYALINIZED NODULE WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIFICATION  O R  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  NEW SUPERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  NEW INFERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  DEEP POSTERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART G  BREAST  RIGHT  NEW MEDIAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART H  BREAST  RIGHT  NEW LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
