Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 50 CLINICAL DATA  Suture at deep margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  TWO NODULES  2 5 CM AND REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE SUPERFICIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IN THE REGION OF THE MASSES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast tissue with a suture designating the deep margin  The deep resection margin is inked black  and the superficial resection margin is inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm in maximal diameter pink gray  firm nodule that abuts the superficial resection margin and is deeply covered only by a thin rim of fibrous tissue  A second separate nodule  0 4cm in maximal diameter is also identified  A representative section of the large nodule in relation to both the superficial and deep resection margin is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  A representative section of the small nodule is frozen as FX 2  now in cassette G  Section code  A  large nodule  previously frozen as FX 1 B F large nodule  additional sections G  small nodule  previously frozen as FX 2 H  small nodule  entirely submitted I  grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST LARGE NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT BREAST  SMALL NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is present as four microscopic foci in twenty slides  Lymphatic invasion is not identified  The examined inked margin is free of infiltrating or in situ carcinoma  however lobular carcinoma in situ is present within a fraction of one millimeter of an inked margin  The entire specimen has been submitted  Dr  Frederick Koerner has examined selected slides on this case and concurs with this diagnosis  Atypical lobular hyperplasia or LCIS is present in approximately half of the submitted slides  2  HYALINIZED CALCIFIED FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 2 8cm fragment of breast tissue with a localizing wire in place  Serial sectioning reveals a 0 4cm area of fatty  tan  gritty tissue corresponding to the terminus of the stereotactic needle biopsy  No frozen section done  The grossly suspicious areas are submitted in A and B and the remainder is submitted in C through T  Gross Description by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS  EXCISION  NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
