d the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  oriented breast biopsy  which is inked as follows  medial half black  lateral blue  anterior green  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white gritty firm nodule  within 0 15cm of the inferior margin  and 0 4cm of the deep resection margin  In the medial aspect of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular  white  firm area  The remaining parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A D  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule in relationship to the closest margins  E H  representative sections of the irregular  white  firm area in relation to the margins I  representative unremarkable breast tissue from the lateral portion of the specimen J  representative uninvolved tissue from the medial portion of the specimen  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  additional margin  stitch on deepest margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink fatty adipose tissue with a suture  The entirely specimen is inked black  and the deep margin  designated by suture  is overlaid with green  The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K through O  Labeled  axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan red fatty adipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in casettes P through T  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                         