er quadrant  which extends to 0 7cm from the anterior margin and 3 3cm from the posterior margin and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm poorly delineated nodular fibrous area in the central lower to mid breast  which extends to 2 0cm from the posterior margin and is 3 5cm from the first described nodule  The lower outer quadrant contains several gritty firm tan foci as large as REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  which extend to 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The lateral tissue contains one small lymph node  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multinodular fibrous area in central lower to mid breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant including firm tan foci   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections  Unfixed  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  left breast   is an 18 x 16 x 4 0cm left mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a 15 x 5 6cm ellipse of skin with an unremarkable areola and nipple  A suture designates the superolateral aspect  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen contains four nodules  The first occupies the  11 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  and extends to 0 2cm from the posterior margin and 0 4cm from the anterior margin  It consists of indurated  triangular  gray white and centrally hemorrhagic tissue  The second sits 4 0cm inferomedial to the first  occupies the  8 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x o 7cm  and extends to 0 4cm from the posterior margin  The mass appears well defined  feels indurated  and consists of tan white and focally hemorrhagic tissue  The third mass occupies the  7 o clock  position at a distance of 0 9cm from the second mass and 6 3cm from the third mass  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and extends to 0 7cm of the posterior margin and 1 5cm of the anterior margin  The final mass occupies the  9 o clock  position  sits 0 7cm superior to the second mass and 3 0cm from the first mass  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and extends to 0 7cm from the posterior margin  It consists of soft  well circumscribed  tan pink tissue  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   11 o clock mass  mass  1  from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue between masses  1 and  2 and between masses  2 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   8 o clock mass  mass  2    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue between mass  2  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass at 7 o clock  mass  3   Unfixed  in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  sentinel lymph node   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of yellow tan soft tissue containing 1 lymph node  which is entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional left axillary sentinel node  247   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fat containing 3 lymph nodes from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  which are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional axillary sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm slightly firm  lymph node  which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional left axillary sentinel node  270   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1   SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 31 48AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 33 59AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  109  to chromosome 17 signals  109  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 53 42PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left   Mastectomy PART C  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART D  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla   Additional Sentinel    Excision PART E  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Additional Sentinel    Excision PART F  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Additional S  report_end  , Unchecked.
