Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  14 MAY 97 at 18 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a left mastectomy specimen  attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin ellipse on the anterior aspect  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left axillary tail  The skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nipple and unremarkable epidermal surface  The breast parenchyma contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow  firm stellate mass in the medial inferior aspect of the specimen  extending to 0 6cm from the posterior  deep  resection margin  3 0cm to the inferior resection margin  3 0cm to the anterior  superficial  margin  4 0cm to the medial resection margin  8 0cm to the superior resection margin  and 4 0cm inferomedial to the nipple areolar complex  The remaining breast parenchyma contains multiple fibrous areas  predominantly in the lateral aspect of the breast  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in dimension  SECTION CODE  A  mass with the closest  posterior deep  resection margin  B D  a cross section of the mass with cut surface inked blue  D F  a cross section of the mass with the cut surface inked blue  G H  inferior lateral fibrous area  I J  superolateral fibrous area  K O  axillary lymph nodes Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  Daniel N Driscoll  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
