Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Rajni V Mandal  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Atypical ductal hyperplasia  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT LOWER UPPER OUTER QUADRANT AREA OF CLIP   EXCISION  1  SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF MULTIFOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  RADIAL SCARS  4  SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  6  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  NOTE  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered small foci in 4 of 10 blocks  GRADE  1  CALCIFICATIONS  In the ductal carcinoma in situ  atypical changes  and benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the superior margin and  0 1cm from the posterior margin  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  BREAST  LEFT UPPER UPPER OUTER QUADRANT AREA OF CALCIFICATION   EXCISION  1  SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH ASSOCIATED MUCOCELE LIKE LESION  FOCAL EARLY MUCINOUS CARCINOMA CANNOT BE EXCLUDED  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  2  2  EXTENSIVE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Several clusters of atypical epithelial cells are present in stromal mucin  raising the possibility of early mucinous carcinoma  Although some of the mucin and some fragments of epithelium appear to be artifactually displaced  the foci in question do not have this appearance  The epithelial clusters of concern in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are no longer present on deeper sections stained for calponin and p63  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the interpretation  Multiple levels examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered small foci in 3 of 10 blocks  GRADE  1  CALCIFICATIONS  Associated with the carcinoma in situ  atypical changes  and benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Present at the anterior margin and  0 1cm from the inferior margin  The mucocele like lesion is also present at the posterior margin and  0 1cm from the anterior and superior margins  and re excision of these margins is suggested as well  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on the  lower upper outer quadrant  specimen  the carcinoma has a similar morphology in both specimens   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  lower upper outer quadrant area of clip   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of yellow fibrofatty tissue  with stitches designating the anterior  lateral  and cephalad  superior  aspects of the specimen per the surgeon  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green and inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal multiple cysts ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm  and surrounding firm parenchyma  A surgical clip is not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of remainder of specimen  submitted sequentially