Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 08 CLINICAL DATA  Approximately nine month history of right breast mass  biopsy positive for malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  1  NOTE  1  All of the resection margins are negative  infiltrating ductal carcinoma extends to within 0 5cm of the closest margin     SCAR  BREAST  RIGHT TISSUE   EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  NOTE  2  All of the resection margins are negative  however  infiltrating ductal carcinoma extends to within 0 1cm of the closest resection margin     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU 5  SOLID TYPE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS      METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2 5 CM DIAMETER  TO 1 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION IS PRESENT  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 03 Consulting Pathologist s   Michael Pins  M D  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast re excision  is a 7 x 5 x 2cm right lumpectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm horizontal skin ellipse  A 2 2cm well healed longitudinal central scar is present within the skin ellipse  The specimen is oriented by a long stitch laterally  and a short stitch superiorly  The semifirm  yellow  fibrofatty tissue is inked yellow  laterally  and black medially  Specimen is serially sectioned  revealing fibrofatty breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white  firm area  grossly abutting the anterior  medially  black inked margin  Located within the superior and inferior aspects of the sample are two biopsy cavities measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  respectively  Section Code A B   closest margins of tumor  mid anterior medial C D   representative sections of lateral breast with skin E   representative section of medial breast with biopsy cavity F   representative section of medial breast G   repres